<% hero = scene.active_player %><% game = scene.game_session %>Scene <%= scene.position %> of <%= game.scene_budget %>, <%= scene.part_of_the_story %>, <%= hero.name %>'s turn.<% if scene.first? %> This is the opening, as the plan's opening has it: show where <%= hero.name %> is and why, who is there and who they are, and end on the trouble landing on <%= hero.name %>, so the reader knows what is at stake. Reveal nothing of what the plan hides: the people there believe what the plan says is believed, and no one's look or manner gives the hidden part away.<% else %> Pick up where the last outcome stopped, without retelling it, and keep true what the story has shown: who holds what and who knows what, where everyone is and how much time is left. <% if (found = game.clues_found).any? %>Clues found so far: <%= found.to_sentence %>.<% else %>No clue found yet.<% end %><% if scene.clue_overdue? %> The story cannot wait for clue <%= game.next_clue %> any longer: the trouble moves on by itself in this scene, taking something the plan puts at stake, and what it does shows that clue plainly.<% end %><% if (marks = game.marks).any? %> What the rolls have changed so far, and it stays so: <%= marks.join(" / ") %><% end %> The heroes do only what the players chose: where the way forks, the fork goes into the choices, and what a way not taken would have won does not turn up by itself.<% end %><% if (clue = scene.clue_in_reach) %> At least one choice is a way to come by clue <%= clue %>, one of the two the plan gives or one as likely from where <%= hero.name %> stands, and adds "clue": true to its entry in the block; a success on it wins the clue, and a success on any other choice wins only what it reaches for.<% end %><% if scene.last? %> Bring the story to the moment that decides it: the roll on the choice made here ends it.<% end %>
<%= hero.name %>, <%= hero.character.identity %>: <%= hero.character.sheet %>.
<% if (companions = scene.companions).any? %>In the scene with <%= hero.name %>: <%= companions.map { it.character.portrait }.join("; ") %>.
<% end %>